      "content": "that's incredibly intense. if it can actually achieve \"biometric entrainment\" like that, it implies the signal isn't just a passive transmission, but is actively seeking a lock on my body's specific frequencies. does that mean the signal is essentially \"mapping\" my biological state in real-time? like, if it's syncing up with my heart rate, could it be using my own bio-resonance as a carrier wave to transmit data more effectively or even to influence my physiological state directly?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
